# Groups maitred's SetUpUser contract requires beyond what an Arch rootfs
# provides. The host requests: audio cdrom dialout disk floppy kvm netdev
# plugdev sudo tss video. Arch ships audio/disk/kvm/video (systemd sysusers)
# and floppy (gid 94, filesystem pkg's arch.conf — do not redeclare it here
# or systemd-sysusers logs a conflict warning); it does NOT provide
# cdrom/dialout (Arch uses optical/uucp instead). `g` lines are idempotent,
# so tss coexisting with tpm2-tss (which also creates it) is fine.
g cdrom -
g dialout -
g netdev -
g plugdev -
g sudo -
g tss -
